/-! # Run unpacking under the NEW boundary (row L5 of docs/parallel/main-theorem-connection.md)

The analogue of `core_reads_inv` / `machine_run_of_core` (ShippingChildRun.lean) with
`O : RefLawsAOpsX MkRefd mref cref` and the invariants `JQ O.quiet D` / `JQCX O D` in place of the old
`RefLaws`, `StartV`, `InvV`.

PROVED here (relative to `O`, `hA` only; the start world is a hypothesis):
* `core_reads_invAX`: a returning run of `synthesizeCombinationalCore declName [] false` from a world
  with `JQ O.quiet D` (and, when `D ≠ 0`, `CacheInvAX O (cv w)`) contains a run of the body
  `synthesizeFromConst …` from a `JQCX O (D + 1)` world (the depth-0 clear establishes the cache
  half; nested runs inherit it);
* `synthesizeFromConst_machine_invAX`, `machine_run_of_coreAX`: on the machine route the body contains
  a run of `synthesizeMachineCertified` starting in a `JQCX O (D + 1)` world (depth ≥ 1).

This is a CONDITIONAL connection to the old endpoints' decomposition. It is not RTL semantic
preservation, not a runtime-fit proof of `O`, and `RealChildAX` / `JQCX` is a history of past
synthesis results, not freshness. -/

